 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all. After each of the first four timeouts, larder waits
+2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds respectively before trying again. A successful attempt returns immediately; if all five time
+out, the final `GatewayTimeout` is raised. The pauses can add 20 seconds to the member's wait on the confirmation
+page, in addition to the time spent waiting for gateway responses.
+
+Previously, three attempts went out back to back within a second. During the gateway's Friday peak, 17:00–19:00,
+all three could land in the same slow minute. One Friday, 58 confirmed pantry orders were left uncharged, and a
+payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway dashboard the next morning. A sandbox replay with the
+current retry schedule suggested that 57 of those 58 would have succeeded. The maintainers accepted the extra wait
+to reduce that manual work. Switching gateways was considered but ruled out because the contract runs to December
+2026. [Issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md) records the discussion.
 
